en  melting before your eyes the episodes  animation supervisor was a familiar face  UK hero k'tano the same guy who  struggled with the tight schedule  episode 24 has the same fate here and  unfortunately he really hasn't fully  grasped Dragon Ball super zart style  which unfortunately results in this so  hopefully this correction will make  things look a little more uniform or at  the very least closer to the character  sheets however despite this being the  second time Cattano features in this  video it unfortunately will be the last  one  - as once the terment of power came  around UK hero katana was demoted back  to a key animator and to be honest I  think that was probably for the best his  movement and animation has never been  bad just his character likeness under  the tight schedule he works much better  when being corrected in my opinion by  another Dragon Ball supervisor but poor  guy regarding the image I'm working on I  decided to rework Goku and Vegeta but  I'm not gonna touch the people in the  background low detail and background  characters isn't an issue and is how  most shows operate after a considerable  amount of time I finished both Goku and  Vegeta with the help and second opinions  of AJ and Trev guiding my hand to the  finish line and with this one done I  guess it's time to jump into the  tournament of power with Trent  [Music]  after a string of great looking episodes  eventually we all knew it had to give  way and episode 1 1 9 was yet another  example of supers atrocious schedule  putting ridiculous strain on its artists  typically as has been the case so far an  episode would only have one animation  supervisor overseeing a bunch of key  animators however in the case of this  episode there are four animation  supervisors and boy does it show for  this particular section with Gohan -  Toma Ono supervised the artwork what's  even more interesting is that within  this code of animation Otto's corrected  the face of Gohan on everything except  the last bit so I guess trebs gonna have  to do it for him ona's artwork encourage  or likeness is actually quite strong so  I think sticking to the character sheets  for this one makes the most sense  instead of trying to replicate a style  like the other ones in the original  Gohan's face needed to be altered as  well as his arms so here it is a fully  finished and corrected Gohan in the  style of tattoo Yoshi Yamamoto and just  like that it's my turn again  this one is bizarre to me coming  straight out of episode 123 we see a  really weird drawing of Vegeta covered  in an aura that almost looks like it's  trying to hide the fact that he has a  massive wonky eye the episode itself was  supervised for Osama Ishikawa who is by  all accounts quite close to the  character sheets with a few notable  differences here and there but even with  massive time constraints I refuse to  believe that  Ishikawa drew this it seems like way too  important of a moment to leave look this  bad but who knows all I know is that I'm  not giving him a wonky eye and I'm gonna  try my best to replicate Ishikawa style  here the entire thing was relatively  easy to draw the major changes I made  were to the face and shoulders I tried  to stop him from being so hunched over  and once again I fixed his wandering eye  additionally thanks to the critiques of  both AJ and Trevor I was able to fix the  minor details that make Ishikawa style  distinct fat ears with angular details  on the inside as well as straight  angular eyes other than that is just  hiding up on the light sources and  making sure everything is in its  preferred place and yeah that's Super  Saiyan blue or Vegeta hopefully this is  an improvement but that brings us to our  final correction and trebs gonna do the  honors episode 129 despite looking  largely okay this episode by all  accounts was a manic situation just  beneath the surface  the animation supervisor was Luigi  karasawa who even supplied some of his  own animation to the episode and it's  some of my favorite stuff from ultra  instant Goku but that couldn't save this  episodes aesthetics completely this shot  of UI Goku is completely owned corrected  and rough possibly from an animator  scrambling to get his work done on time  this episode looks as consistent as it  does only because half of the run time  consists of Bank or reused animation  reused or Bank animation is the  animation that would have been created  for an earlier episode but was  repurposed facilitate this episode's  needs thankfully this close-up of UI  Goku is a rather simple fix the goal of  this particular correction is to forget  closer to Kurosawa style which can be  seen throughout the entire episode and I  think this correction helps bring this  drawing in line with that aesthetic in  this video myself AJ and Trev spent our  time this week correct in the work of  other talented artists ten drawings in  total but what we didn't show you was  how long each drawing took us to create  keep in mind that we are working without  massive time constraints using  oftentimes the reference of the original  image to carry some of the work and we  are only working on a single frame the  animators that worked on these had to  produce hundreds of these drawings from  scratch with virtually no time at all  the average episode of Dragon Ball super  will contain between three thousand five  hundred and five thousand unique  drawings all prepared by these artists  my hope with this video is to point out  that there are real human beings  genuinely trying their very best to do  their job well under harrowing  circumstances speaking as an artist  myself I can't imagine how awful it must  have felt to be under that sort of time  constraint to create artwork for an  extremely popular property only to have  the entire world laughs at your efforts  and regrettably I was part of that  problem too so I'd like to take this  opportunity to say I'm sorry I would  like to thank Trev for supplying some  incredible artwork for this project and  I would like to thank AJ for the same as  well as providing the vast majority of  information in this video  they are both extremely talented and you  can find their social media in the  description down below go follow them  but that will do it for this week guys I  hope you enjoyed the video I'll see you  all next week and thank you so much for  watching  in between spam pausing and zooming in  claims that this was episode 5 tear and  call the animators to be fired this is  such disgusting and embarrassing  behavior and it's not even close to  reality if this issue stop  [Music]
 

